audio music - [volume="-2.0" loop="true"]
[Alarm beeping]
join Lizzy (Close Up) center [animation="Fade In Up" extra_data="show Hips"]
Lizzy: -AaAAAAAAAAHHHHHHHHHH-
...
update Lizzy (Close Up) center [length="2.0" wait="true" extra_data="show Loop3, hide Hips"]
VO: My guts are still firmly inside of me, where they belong.
VO: I guess that’s one of the advantages of being stuck in a time loop.
update Lizzy [extra_data="hide Loop3, show Side"]
VO: Attacking Lady MacDeath directly won’t get me anywhere...
VO: Well.
VO: I’m out of ideas.
...
join "Strike Ball" (Shakespeare) midleft
VO: Oh, hey, I still have this heavily annotated book.
VO: Maybe I could ransom it.
audio "res://audio/Phone ringing sound.mp3"


[PHONE RINGING]
leave "Strike Ball"
VO: Valerie’s calling me?
VO: I didn't think she'd ever use her phone again after the thing with the phone ghost.
join Valerie (Phone) left
update Lizzy midright [length="0.2" move_time="0.2"]
Valerie: Elizabeth, it’s Valerie.
Lizzy: I know,
Lizzy: I have caller ID.
Valerie: Good for you.
Valerie: I called to tell you that I remember everything.
update Lizzy [animation="Bounce" wait="true"]
Lizzy: WHAT! Really?
Lizzy: That’s amazing!
Lizzy: Well, I mean, it sucks because now we’re both stuck in this time loop,
Lizzy: But at least I’m not alone anymore!
update Valerie [animation="Tada"]
Valerie: Your unbeatable spirit allowed me to retain my memories from the previous loop.
Lizzy: thank god for my unbeatable spirit.
Valerie: and good news, My research may have uncovered a possible solution.
Lizzy: Phew, I was starting to think I’d have to keep doing random stuff until something changed.
Lizzy: I'm not that good at coming up with new ideas.
Valerie: Meet me in the library. I’m giving you permission to skip your final exam.
leave Valerie [animation="Slide Out Down"]
Lizzy: Oh, don’t worry, I don’t need your permission.
VO: ...
VO: She hung up.
VO: Her phone etiquette is terrible.
leave --All--
